From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: nt36532: use the OEM video traffic mode for Liuqin

Both Liuqin M81 panel descriptions in OS2.0.6.0.VMYCNXM select burst_mode.
The inherited Pipa description selects non-burst sync-event traffic instead.
Select burst traffic only in the Liuqin description, retaining all command
tables, lane settings, mode timings, clock flags, supplies and delays.

This aligns the traffic mode with the OEM configuration; burst mode alone
did not resolve intermittent first-enable corruption during hardware tests.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36532.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36532.c
@@ -525,7 +525,8 @@ static const struct panel_desc liuqin_desc = {
 		.block_pred_enable = true,
 	},
 	.format = MIPI_DSI_FMT_RGB888,
-	.mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO | MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS,
+	.mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO | MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST |
+		      MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS,
 	.drm_mode = liuqin_mode_120,
 	.init_sequence = pipa_init_sequence,
 	.reset_sequence = liuqin_reset,
